A* Pathfinder: Data Structures Visualizer:
A sleek, interactive web-based tool designed to visualize the A*  Search Algorithm and its variants on a dynamic graph. Built with vanilla 
JavaScript and HTML5 Canvas, this project allows users to build custom topologies and watch how the algorithm explores nodes in real-time.
🚀 Features
 Interactive Graph Construction:
 Add Nodes: Click anywhere on the canvas to create new vertices.
 Add Edges: Connect nodes with weighted, directed edges.Weights are automatically calculated based on Euclidean distance.
 Drag & Drop: Reposition nodes dynamically to see how the heuristic values change.
 Delete Mode: Easily remove nodes or edges from your layout.
 Algorithm Variants:
 A* (Euclidean): Uses straight-line distance.
 A* (Manhattan): Uses L1 distance (ideal for grid-like layouts).
 Dijkstra's Algorithm: Runs the search with $h(n) = 0$, focusing purely on path cost.
 Real-time Metrics: Track the "Open Set," "Closed Set," total nodes explored, and the final path cost (f = g + h).
 Visualization Controls: Adjustable animation speed from "Slow" to "Fast."

🛠️ Technical Overview
The visualizer is built using a modern "Dark Mode" aesthetic powered by the Syne and Space Mono typefaces.
The A* Equation
The algorithm selects the next node to explore based on the formula:
  f(n) = g(n) + h(n)
 g(n): The actual cost from the start node to the current node n.
 h(n): The heuristic (estimated) cost from $n$ to the goal.
 f(n): The total estimated cost of the cheapest solution through n.

Project Structure
 index.html: The structural layout including the sidebar controls and the main canvas.
 style.css: Custom CSS Variables for easy skinning and a responsive grid layout.
 script.js: The core logic, including the A* implementation, canvas rendering engine, and event handlers.

